      "id": "claim_f0f1d854793049f99241a19d4a22656d",
      "statement": "The governing validation rule is cumulative proof with minimal live coupling: a downstream test reuses prior PASS evidence where an earlier capability is a real prerequisite and creates only the smallest temporary integration needed to prove its own contract, and temporary wiring never becomes production architecture.",
